      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, a swollen battery, you say? Well, it's like a mischievous goblin that has overstayed its welcome in your phone. First, you must banish it from your device, as it can be quite the troublemaker. Gently remove the phone from your pocket, as if you're coaxing a shy goblin out of hiding. Then, carefully place the phone in a non-conductive container, like a box of old goblin bones, to prevent any electrical mishaps. \n\nNow, for the disposal, it's like sending a goblin back to the goblin realm. Contact your local electronics recycling center, or look for a certified e-waste disposal service. They will handle the goblin with the care it deserves, ensuring it doesn't wreak havoc on the environment. Remember, never attempt to dispose of it yourself, as it could lead to a goblin uprising in the form of a fire or explosion. Stay safe, and may your phone be free of goblin-like issues in the future!",
